% review-id: first-tunes-7-oh-susanna
% review-from: samples
% review-status: pending
% review-categories: racism, violence, context
% review-findings: No words in the file. Stephen Foster wrote it in 1848 for blackface minstrel shows, and his original second verse uses a racial slur in a joke about an explosion that kills five hundred Black people. Anyone who looks up the words can find it.
% review-suggestion: Keep it out of the course. If a teacher wants the tune, play the melody only and teach the minstrel history with it; never the original words.
